  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1131 AM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nThe warming trend will continue over the next few days, with \ntemperatures around 10 degrees warmer than the seasonal averages\nWednesday through Saturday despite some increase in cloudiness.\nBreezy south winds most afternoons will result in some limited\nfire weather concerns, mainly across parts of northeast Oklahoma.\n\nA cold front will move across the area Saturday evening and\novernight bringing a chance for showers and possibly a\nthunderstorm or two. Rainfall amounts look to mostly remain on the\nlight side as of now. Temperatures will fall back to near the\nseasonal averages Sunday through Tuesday following the passage of\nthis front. A stronger storm system may bring a chance of rain\naround Tuesday of next week, but uncertainty is high regarding the\ntrack of this system and its potential impacts in our area.",
